Install Jenkins on Ubuntu VM
Step 1: Update Ubuntu
Shell
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
Step 2: Install Java (Jenkins Requirement)

Jenkins requires Java.

Shell
sudo apt install openjdk-17-jdk -y

Verify:

Shell
java -version

Expected output:

Shell
openjdk version "17"
Step 3: Add Jenkins Repository Key
Shell
curl -fsSL https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2023.key | sudo tee \
/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc > /dev/null
Step 4: Add Jenkins Repository
Shell
echo deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] \
https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/ | sudo tee \
/etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list > /dev/null
Step 5: Install Jenkins
Shell
sudo apt update
sudo apt install jenkins -y
Step 6: Start Jenkins
Shell
sudo systemctl start jenkins
sudo systemctl enable jenkins

Check status:

Shell
sudo systemctl status jenkins

You should see:

Shell
active (running)
Step 7: Allow Port 8080

If UFW firewall is enabled:

Shell
sudo ufw allow 8080
sudo ufw reload
Step 8: Open Jenkins

Check VM IP:

Shell
ip addr

or

Shell
hostname -I

Open in browser:

Plain Text
http://<VM-IP>:8080

Example:

Plain Text
http://192.168.1.100:8080
Step 9: Get Initial Admin Password
Shell
sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword

Copy the password and paste it into the Jenkins web page.

Useful Jenkins Commands

Start:

Shell
sudo systemctl start jenkins

Stop:

Shell
sudo systemctl stop jenkins

Restart:

Shell
sudo systemctl restart jenkins

Status:

Shell
