8080 another app running

If another application is already using port 8080, you have 2 options:

Option 1: Find and stop the process on 8080

Check what's using 8080:

Shell
sudo ss -tulpn | grep 8080

or

Shell
sudo lsof -i :8080

Example output:

Shell
tcp LISTEN 0 4096 *:8080 *:* users:(("java",pid=1234))

Kill the process:

Shell
sudo kill -9 1234

Then restart Jenkins:

Shell
sudo systemctl restart jenkins
Option 2: Change Jenkins Port

Edit Jenkins configuration:

Shell
sudo nano /etc/default/jenkins

Find:

Shell
HTTP_PORT=8080

Change to:

Shell
HTTP_PORT=8081

Save:

Ctrl + X
Y
Enter

Restart Jenkins:

Shell
sudo systemctl restart jenkins

Check:

Shell
sudo systemctl status jenkins

Open:

Plain Text
http://<VM-IP>:8081
Quick Command to See All Used Ports
Shell
sudo ss -tulpn

or only common DevOps ports:

Shell
sudo ss -tulpn | grep -E '8080|8081|3000|9090|9000'

Since you've installed Prometheus and Grafana, it's common that:

Grafana → 3000
Prometheus → 9090
Jenkins → 8080 (or change to 8081)
ArgoCD → 8080/443 (sometimes)

Run:

Shell
sudo lsof -i :8080

and paste the output here. I can tell you exactly which application is occupying port 8080.

